$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: To a benzene solution of 1 (4 mg, 8 micromol)
was added 4-fluoroiodobenzene (4.5 μL, 40 μmol) followed by 2-thiocresol
or 2,6-dimethylthiophenol (1.1 μL, 8.8 μmol). The red solution turned
bright yellow upon addition and brown within 5 min. n-pentane was added
to the suspension after 24 h at RT The liquid phase was evaporated to
give a reddish solid which was purified on silica gel column to yield the
corresponding biarylsulfide (from 2-thiocresol). The solid phase
contained complex 8. (2,6-dimethylphenyl)(4-fluorophenyl) sulfide, from
2,6-dimethylthiophenol: 1.7 mg, 92% yield); complex 8, yield (ca. 80%).
(2,6-dimethylphenyl)(4-fluorophenyl) sulfide: 1H NMR 7.32-7.24 (m, Ar-H,
3H), 7.01-6.93 (m, Ar-H, 4H), 2.52 (s, CH3, 6H); 13C{1H} 160.80 (d, JFC =
243.2 Hz, C-F), 143.76 (s), 133.13 (d, J= 3.2 Hz), 129.42 (s), 128.64
(s), 127.60 (d, JFC = 7.7 Hz), 116.17 (s), 115.95 (s), 21.91 (s); 19F{1H}
-117.28 (s); EI-MS M+ (Calc. for C14H13FS) 232 (232).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
