$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM A solution of p-thiocresol in benzene (0.5 ml) was added dropwise to a
benzene solution (1 ml) of 7 (2.0 mg, 3.7 μmol) and 4-fluoroiodobenzene
(2.1 μL, 18.0 μmol). After 15 min at RT, the crude was filtered through a
plug of celite followed by three washes of the remaining solid with
n-pentane (1 ml). The benzene and n-pentane phases were combined and
evaporated to give an orange solid which was purified on silica gel to
give (4-fluorophenyl)(p-tolyl)sulfide. The remaining yellow solid was
dissolved in dichloromethane and the resulting yellow solution was
evaporated to give 6. 6, yellow solid, yield (2.0 mg, 80%);
(4-fluorophenyl)(p-tolyl)sulfide, colorless oil, yield (0.6 mg, 80%).
(4-fluorophenyl)(p-tolyl)sulfide: 1H NMR 7.32-7.28 (m, Ar-H, 2H),
7.25-7.20 (m, Ar-H, 2H), 7.14-7.09 (m, Ar-H, 2H), 7.02-6.95 (m, Ar- H,
2H), 2.33 (s, CH3, 3H); 13C{1H} 162.18 (d, JFC = 247.0 Hz, C-F), 137.47
(s), 132.9 (d, J= 7.9 Hz), 131.37 (s), 130.19 (s), 128.48 (s), 116.47
(s), 116.26 (s), 29.85 (s); 19F{1H} -114.45 (s); EI-MS M+ (Calc. for
C13H11FS) 218 (218). 6: 1H NMR 8.71 (d, J= 8.5 Hz, Ar-H, 1H), 8.62 (d, J=
8.5 Hz, Ar-H, 1H), 8.14 (d, J= 8.1 Hz, Ar-H, 1H), 8.06 (d, J= 7.2 Hz,
Ar-H, 2H), 7.76 (t, J= 7.8 Hz, Ar-H, 2H), 7.44-7.38 (m, Ar-H, 2H), 6.93
(t, J= 9.0 Hz, Ar-H, 2H), 4.69 (d, JPH = 9.5 Hz, CH2-P, 2H), 3.09-3.03
(dq, J= 7.0, 2.9 Hz, CH3CH2S, 2H), 1.40 (d, JPH = 15.2 Hz, (CH3)3C-P,
18H), 1.29 (t, J= 7.20 Hz, CH3CH2S, 3H); 13C{1H} 165.83 (d, J= 2.3 Hz),
162.55 (s), 160.14 (s), 147.57 (d, J= 1.4 Hz), 140.56 (s), 137.40 (d, J=
3.0 Hz), 137.34 (d, J= 3.0 Hz), 137.13 (d, J= 2.6 Hz), 133.71 (t, J= 2.2
Hz), 131.33 (s), 130.94 (d ,J= 1.6 Hz), 129.38 (s), 128.05 (s), 124.65
(d, J= 9.0 Hz), 115.34 (d, J= 18.4 Hz), 40.24 (d, J= 22.7 Hz, CH2-P),
37.46 (d, J= 16.9 Hz, (CH3)3C-P), 35.62 (s, CH3CH2S), 29.51 (d, J= 4.2
Hz, (CH3)3C-P), 15.24 (s, CH3CH2S); 19F{1H} -119.78 (s); 31P{1H} 72.09
(s); ESI-HRMS M+ (Calc. for C26H34FNPPdS) 546.1171 (546.1174).
